			"notes": "## New\n- **Velo Client capes.** Shows the capes Velo Client users wear, including animated ones. It reads Velo's public list of online players without signing in to Velo. Turn it off with **Velo Capes** (`velo` in config.json). It turns itself off when Velo Client is installed.\n- **Essential clothing hides only the skin pixels it covers**, as in Essential, instead of hiding whole outer-layer parts. Works with 3D Skin Layers and the Feminine Gender Mod.\n- **Essential sleeves, gloves and bracelets show on your first-person arm.**\n- **Built-in updater.** When a newer Clientmetics is released, you're offered it as a OneConfig notification (or on the title screen without OneConfig). **Update** downloads it from GitHub, checks it against the release's SHA-256, and installs it when you close the game. Turn it off with **Check for Updates** (`checkForUpdates` in config.json).\n\n## Note\nThe first-launch notice now mentions Velo, so it will ask you again once."
		},
